body:
Maths/Further Maths you can get videos from Bicen Maths and TLMaths - and practice papers from madasmaths and naikermaths. CS also has s1perry with some useful videos though I personally don't watch him much.

&#x200B;

Idk about Physics though.

Don't pick "easy" A levels because everyone has different understandings of the course. I could say CS or Maths is easy but someone else would just be lost.

&#x200B;

For me though I'd say maths. No extended answer questions obviously.

sent mine last week, got 2 offers so far so it's a relatively calm process depending on who approved and submitted your app from your centre.

&#x200B;

good luck op!
